import Foundation

// Files, as bytes, for `ImageTests.kira` and `InflateTests.kira`.
//
// Each blob is a real file that a second implementation also reads, and the
// values the tests assert were taken from that second implementation rather
// than from this one — so a test failing here means the two disagree, which is
// the only thing a decoder can be right or wrong about. Holding them as arrays
// rather than as files on disk is what lets the suite run wherever it is
// launched from and on a backend with no filesystem.
//
// Naming: everything in the harness shares one flat namespace, so these carry
// the `image`/`inflate` prefix their tests do.

